{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":61685,"duration_api_ms":57612,"ttft_ms":8755,"ttft_stream_ms":1696,"time_to_request_ms":257,"num_turns":8,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"This repo has no Dockerfile, no CI/CD workflow (no .github/workflows), and no custom observability stack — it deploys to Vercel with Supabase as the backing service, and checks run locally/manually via `npm run verify`. For status-page, infra's scope is narrow: deciding how 'environment' and 'version' are sourced and wired as env vars/build metadata so the backend endpoint can read them safely, without leaking secrets or build details. The endpoint itself and the page are application code owned by backend/frontend roles.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"Vercel project environment variables\",\n    \".env.example documentation\",\n    \"docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md (deployment/env conventions)\",\n    \"next.config.ts (if build-time metadata injection is needed)\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Decide and document the source of truth for 'current application environment': use Vercel's built-in VERCEL_ENV (production/preview/development) rather than inventing a new variable, since it's already populated by the platform with no extra wiring.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Decide and document the source of truth for 'backend version': recommend either package.json's version field (read server-side via process.env.npm_package_version or a small import) or VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (short SHA) exposed server-side only. No new build step should be required unless the git SHA route needs explicit wiring in next.config.ts.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Update .env.example and docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md with a short note on which env vars the status endpoint relies on, so local dev behaves consistently with Vercel Preview/Production.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\", \"infra-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement a GET status endpoint (e.g. app/api/status/route.ts) returning API availability, version, and environment, using the env/var contract defined in infra-1/infra-2. Decide whether 'availability' includes a live Supabase connectivity check.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\", \"infra-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"frontend-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the user-facing status page under app/ that fetches and renders the status endpoint response.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"frontend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"docs-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the new endpoint and page per repo convention (docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md entry + relevant guide section).\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1\", \"frontend-1\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Environment field in the status response should map directly to Vercel's VERCEL_ENV values ('production' | 'preview' | 'development'), not a custom enum, to avoid drift between platform and app.\",\n    \"Version field should be a single build-time-resolved string (package.json version or short git SHA) decided once in infra-2 and consumed read-only by the backend route — not re-derived per request.\",\n    \"No secrets, internal hostnames, or dependency version numbers should be included in the status response body.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Information disclosure: exposing precise version/commit SHA or internal environment details publicly can help an attacker fingerprint the stack. Recommend minimal, coarse-grained fields only.\",\n    \"If 'API availability' is implemented as a live Supabase ping, it could count against connection limits or add latency if the page/endpoint is polled frequently or cached incorrectly — needs explicit cache-control (likely no-store) decided with backend.\",\n    \"No CI/CD pipeline currently exists in this repo; if the team wants automated post-deploy smoke checks against the new endpoint, that's a new infrastructure addition requiring explicit authorization per AGENTS.md, not an implicit part of this feature.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Not an infra deliverable, but flagging: backend should unit-test the status route's response shape per environment var combination (set via test env mocks).\",\n    \"No automated CI exists to run these tests on push; manual `npm run verify` (or `npm run test`) remains the only enforcement mechanism unless the team explicitly requests a CI pipeline be added.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Should 'version' be the npm package.json version (manually bumped) or the Vercel git commit SHA (always accurate, less human-readable)? This is a product decision, not purely technical.\",\n    \"Should 'API availability' mean the endpoint merely responding (trivial), or an active Supabase/database connectivity check (adds latency and a new failure mode)? This determines whether infra needs to coordinate on Supabase credentials/timeouts.\",\n    \"Is this status page purely informational for internal/admin use, or should it eventually back an external uptime monitor (e.g., UptimeRobot/BetterStack) hitting this endpoint? No such integration exists today — out of scope unless requested.\",\n    \"Given there's no .github/workflows or Dockerfile in this repo, is any CI/CD or containerization work expected as part of this feature, or is Vercel's existing git-based deploy sufficient?\"\n  ]\n}\n```","st